dear Hans we hope you're having a  wonderful time shoveling manure in the  Southern Isles you got what you deserved  you're 12 brothers made sure of that now  while some might refer to you as the  true villain of frozen we wouldn't give  you that much credit you tried to take  over Arundale in the sneakiest way  possible but you were no match for Anna  and Elsa's sisterly love  now Maleficent that's a villain you  could be a henchman at best unlike the  many Disney movies that came before it  the frozen franchise doesn't have any  real villains Disney totally flipped the  script on this one and that just might  be why fans can't get enough of frozen 1  &amp; 2 keep watching to find out who the  real villains are or rather what they  are there were a few bad apples in the  first frozen film but we wouldn't go so  far as to name them the villains of the  franchise sure Hans tricked Anna into  falling in love with him and tried to  take over arendelle but there was a  greater evil at work Hans and the Duke  of weselton tried to weasel their way  into arendelle's good graces but their  attempts fell flat  unlike most Disney Princess movies  frozen didn't follow the usual template  sure Anna and Elsa lost their parents at  the beginning of the film and Anna did  meet a charming Prince but Elsa didn't  get rescued by a knight in shining armor  instead she was saved by a princess in  shining ice hands in the Duke of  weselton may have stirred the pot but it  was Elsa's fear that was to blame for  the series of unfortunate events that  take place in frozen after nearly  costing Anna her life when they were  just kids Elsa gave in to fear and it  swallowed her whole  she was so afraid of her powers that she  repressed them and it totally backfired  on her Elsa never learned to step into  her power or hone her craft she saw  herself as a monster and an outcast and  her fear grew to new heights after she  lost her parents Elsa's powers are  linked to her emotions which is why King  Agner taught her to conceal don't feel  so while Elsa managed to keep it  together during her coronation ceremony  she couldn't contain her rage when Anna  pushed her buttons in front of their  guests and then said  the secret Elsa had tried so hard to  keep was now public knowledge by the end  of frozen Elsa would realize that love  was the antidote of fear she realized  this when Anna chose to sacrifice  herself to save her  Anna's act of true love was enough to  thaw her frozen heart when Anna was  moments away from Kristoff she noticed  Hans creeping up on Elsa sword and hand  he was about to strike so Anna had to  act fast  she chose love instead of fear prompting  Elsa to do the same if it hadn't been  for Elsa's fear the true villain of the  story Anna and Elsa would have never  lived a sheltered life and Anna wouldn't  have fallen for honza's tricks nor would  she have accepted his proposal so it's  plain to see that fear was the culprit  not Hans but we're not letting him off  the hook that easily and neither are his  brothers did you know that frozen is  loosely based on Hans Christian  Andersen's fairy tale The Snow Queen  well in that version The Snow Queen  herself is the villain of the story  Disney chose to revamp the 19th century  fairy tale but during some parts of the  film Elsa could be seen as the villain  of her story too after all she did set  off an eternal winter lucky for the  people of arendelle  else that doesn't have a bad bone in her  body I woke the magical spirit at the  enchanted forest okay that's definitely  not what I thought you were gonna say  we've already established that the real  villain of frozen was fear itself but  what about frozen - at first glance you  might think that AG nars father was the  villain after all he's the one who  decided to betray the North ultras and  his actions angered the spirits of the  forest which led to the fog barrier  being put up but Elsa and Anna's  grandfather's role was so minor he  couldn't possibly be the big bat of  frozen - so instead of focusing on good  versus evil  Disney chose to focus on a completely  different storyline where as frozen was  all about overcoming fear its sequel was  all about embracing change and finding  where you belong frozen - taught us how  important it is to be true to who you  are for years Elsa knew that she wasn't  where she was met  - b-but she felt an obligation to the  throne so she stuck around despite all  the pain it caused her unlike her  grandfather Elsa didn't succumb to fear  she put everything on the line and  journeyed into the unknown to find  herself she didn't let the expectations  of other people hold her back from who  she was meant to be we love how Disney  is flipping the script on these typical  Disney Princess movies villains aren't  the main focus anymore instead Disney is  focusing on the emotional journeys of  their main characters from overcoming  fear to righting wrongs to figuring out  where they belong and as a result Disney  protagonists are more relatable than  ever here are the things we love  catching up with all things Disney and  Nickelodeon so hit that subscribe button  if you do - and don't forget to click  the bell while you're at it this way  you'll never miss another video if  you're tuning into this on your mobile  turn on notifications on your YouTube  settings and that's a wrap on why frozen  movies don't have any villains we hope  you enjoyed our video before you go tell  us who your top three Disney villains  are in the comments below thanks for  watching don't forget to give this video  a big thumbs up we'll catch you next  time on the things
 

